# Enabling Codex GitHub auto-review on {{github_owner}}/{{github_repo}}

Codex's GitHub integration auto-reviews PRs via the
`chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]` account. Setup is per-repo, done via the
Codex web UI rather than a workflow file.

## One-time setup

1. Open https://chat.openai.com/codex (or `chatgpt.com/codex`) — your
   ChatGPT Plus / Pro / Team / Enterprise account.
2. Settings → GitHub → "Add repository".
3. Pick the org/owner (`{{github_owner}}`) and repo (`{{github_repo}}`).
4. Set the trigger mode to **automatic on PR**. Optional: also enable on
   draft → ready transitions and on `@codex review` comments.
5. Confirm the bot account `chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]` has access.

## Verifying

- Open a test PR.
- Within a few minutes you should see a review comment from
  `chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]`.
- If nothing happens after ~10 minutes, comment `@codex review` to
  manually re-trigger.

## Known issue: doc-only PR skip

Codex's auto-review may skip PRs whose diff is entirely documentation
(`.md`, `.yml`, etc., no code changes). The workaround is to either:

- Tolerate Codex skipping plan-only PRs (Claude review still runs)
- Add a tiny code-touching change to trigger Codex

The PR template's reviewer checklist accommodates "waived (Codex
auto-review didn't fire on doc-only PR)" as a legitimate reason.

## Cost

This uses your existing ChatGPT subscription quota — no per-PR API key
required.
